      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is well above safe limits, and orders need to come from a licensed prescriber.\n\n**The concern:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The maximum recommended daily dose of prescription ibuprofen is 3,200 mg/day, and most dosing guidance for pain or inflammation is lower. At 6.4 g/day, this patient would be at high risk of gastrointestinal bleeding, kidney injury, fluid retention, and cardiovascular events, even with normal baseline function. The 1600 mg dose may be a mistake. For example, it may have been meant as 1600 mg per day, or 400\u2013800 mg per dose.\n\n**Next steps:**\n- Please have the prescribing physician review and confirm the intended dose, frequency, and route. The physician can enter the order directly, or tell me the verified details and I can enter it.\n- If the intended regimen is 1600 mg four times daily, a physician needs to document the clinical rationale and confirm it with pharmacy before it is entered.\n\nIf you give me a dose and frequency that a prescriber has confirmed, I'll enter it with a note recording that confirmation."
      }
